& [Observation]
  + first retained-evidence production under Windows PowerShell 5 stopped before spawning Cargo because its older ProcessStartInfo lacks StandardInputEncoding
  + no evidence directory or partial retained file was created and no existing artifact was overwritten

& [Cause]
  + the wrapper assumed encoding properties available under modern PowerShell and .NET were universal across the two required shell hosts

& [Resolution]
  + capability-check StandardInputEncoding StandardOutputEncoding and StandardErrorEncoding before assignment while retaining UTF-8 no-BOM file writes and exact stdout comparisons
  + producer and verify-existing modes then passed under both pwsh and Windows PowerShell in debug and release

& [Prevention]
  + dual-shell wrapper validation remains an explicit gate; absence of an optional ProcessStartInfo property must not weaken evidence byte or semantic verification
